#!bovnar 1.1
# currencies.bvnr — single source of truth for the currency catalogue.
#
# HOW THIS WORKS
#   Hand-edited. gen_currencies.py (at the repo root) regenerates the C
#   catalogue from this file on every build; never edit the generated
#   *.gen.{h,inc}. To add, remove, or change a currency, edit a record below
#   and rebuild.
#
# STABLE IDS (ABI)
#   .id is the value_base_unit_t enum value. Append-only: NEVER renumber or
#   reuse an id. Currencies are the 90 BLOCK: ids 900000..909999, contiguous
#   from 900000, fiat first and then crypto. The catalogue is POSITIONAL — a
#   currency's slot IS its enum value minus 900000 — so records MUST stay in
#   ascending .id order; the C table's O(1) index depends on it.
#
#   A new currency of EITHER kind appends at the end with the next free id.
#   Fiat happens to run before crypto here, and the fiat rows happen to be
#   alphabetical, but neither is a contract: bvn_unit_is_fiat and
#   bvn_unit_is_crypto read the .is_crypto column of the row rather than
#   testing which sub-range the id falls in, so the ordering carries no
#   meaning and appending never renumbers anything.
#
# FIELDS (one record per currency)
#   .id            value_base_unit_t enum value (stable, ordered; see above)
#   .code          ISO 4217 / ticker, 3-4 upper-case letters (e.g. "USD", "BTC")
#   .numeric_code  ISO 4217 numeric code (0 for crypto)
#   .minor_unit    decimal places (2 USD, 0 JPY, 8 BTC, 18 ETH)
#   .is_crypto     true for crypto assets, false for fiat
#   .name          human-readable name

.schema_version = <uint:16> 1;

